# cloud-dev (fully cloud-based)

This repository's **cloud-dev** branch is the **full cloud-based** development track. Agents and humans may work from **different locations** (Cursor Cloud, mobile, CI, local PC) with **GitHub as the single source of truth**.

## Branch role

| Branch | Use |
|---|---|
| `cloud-dev` | Cloud Agent, mobile, cursor.com |
| `local-dev` | Local PC development |
| `main` | Production — stable only |
| `feature/*` | Single task branches |

- Work on **`cloud-dev`** (or `feature/*` branched from it) for cloud/mobile sessions
- Work on **`local-dev`** for local PC sessions
- Sync via `git pull` / `git push` — never keep code on one machine only
- Never commit secrets (`.env`)

## Zero vendor / IDE traces in shipped work

When writing **code, comments, docs, commit messages, PR text, UI copy, or assets**:

- Do **not** mention Cursor, Cursor Cloud, Cursor Agent, or any IDE product name
- Do **not** add co-author trailers, "Made-with" lines, or AI attribution
- Do **not** leave tool fingerprints in source or public docs
- Use **AnantaOne** project identity only — not personal or vendor branding

Internal `.cursor/rules/` files may reference tooling only to **block** attribution.

## Cloud workflow

1. `git checkout cloud-dev && git pull origin cloud-dev`
2. Create `feature/*` branch for the task
3. Commit and push often
4. Merge feature → `cloud-dev`, then sync `local-dev` on PC
5. Merge to `main` only when tested on both environments

See `docs/GIT-WORKFLOW.md` for full sync rules.
